<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian sugar crush - week to July 19.</title>
<headline>Australian sugar crush - week to July 19.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's sugar cane crush totalled 1,711,982 tonnes in the week ended July 19, bringing the crush so far this season to 7.27 million tonnes, grower organisation CANEGROWERS said.</p>
<p>This is slightly lower than 7.37 million tonnes crushed at the same time last year. CANEGROWERS reported for crushing week seven of the 1997 season that average commercial cane sugar (ccs) content was 12.98 percent.</p>
<p>The figures do not include cane crushed in the Ord River region of Western Australia.  </p>
<p>Australian sugar cane crush by region for the week ended July 19 as reported by CANEGROWERS in tonnes.</p>
<p>CCS = Commercial Cane Sugar (sugar content percent)-</p>
